Key Observations
The client used an ephemeral source port.
The server used TCP port 443 for HTTPS communication.
The SYN packet contained the SYN flag.
The SYN-ACK packet contained both SYN and ACK flags.
The final packet contained the ACK flag.
The SYN packet had a relative sequence number of 0.
The SYN-ACK acknowledged the client's SYN with acknowledgment number 1.
The final ACK acknowledged the server's SYN with acknowledgment number 1.
Each direction of TCP communication maintains its own sequence-number space.
